WEBVTT

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:07.300
The cylinder had been left behind by the man who kept the garret before me.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.551
He had gone in the night, owing a fortnight,

00:00:10.551 --> 00:00:13.840
and had taken his boots and his hat and nothing else.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.100
Mr.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.310
Wetherby let the room to me on the Tuesday,

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.062
and on the Wednesday I found the cylinder in the drawer of the washstand,

00:00:21.062 --> 00:00:23.940
wrapped in a flannel that smelled of camphor and tallow.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.440
The label was brown with age.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.320
It read, in a thin clerkly hand, Larkspur, No. 1.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.296
The phonograph stood on the sill, under the window,

00:00:35.296 --> 00:00:37.280
its brass horn turned to the room.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:42.552
It had come with the garret, like the damp patch over the bed and the sixth stair

00:00:42.552 --> 00:00:44.140
that cried out when trodden.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:45.960
I had never wound it.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.935
I had my bell to wind, and my father's ledger to puzzle over,

00:00:49.935 --> 00:00:54.060
and on that night I wanted only to sit and not think of the quarter-day.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:58.500
The fog had been in the Larkspur since four o'clock.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.930
It stood against the glass and gave the lamp a yellow ring,

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:06.640
and below me the foghorns on the river called to one another, one low, one lower.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.340
I slid the cylinder onto the mandrel.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.940
I turned the crank eleven times, because I count what I turn.

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:14.540
I lowered the stylus.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.440
First came hissing, and then a breath, taken close.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:21.580
"Forgive me," said a voice.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:23.240
"Please.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.140
I have carried it so long."

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.660
It was my voice.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.880
I do not say it resembled mine.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.208
I know my own voice as I know the weight of the rope in my hands: the flat northern

00:01:34.208 --> 00:01:36.600
vowels, the catch before a hard consonant.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.660
I put my fingers to my throat and felt nothing move there.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.000
The speaker went on, tender and low, as a man speaks to a sick child.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.180
"I never meant the water to take him.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.260
I held his sleeve as long as I could.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:54.280
You must believe that I held it.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.160
Say that you forgive me for the drowning, and I will ask for nothing more."

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:00.220
I stood up.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.680
The chair went over behind me.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.640
I did not set it right.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.119
There was a silence on the cylinder, and in it the sound of a clock,

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:13.500
a slow clock with a loose pendulum, such as hangs in the parlour downstairs.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:19.020
Then a second speaker answered, calm, unhurried, and dry as paper.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:20.740
"I forgive you, Desmond.

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:21.680
Of course I do.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:22.720
Sit down now.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.660
It is finished."

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.420
It was Mr.

00:02:25.460 --> 00:02:26.620
Reginald Wetherby.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.248
I had heard him on the stairs not two hours before,

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:31.360
saying that the gas was not to be wasted.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.280
He had said nothing to me of water, or of a sleeve, or of forgiveness.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.020
I have never drowned any man.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.580
I have never stood on a quay at night and watched a hand go under.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.260
I have rung the bell of St.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.714
Anselm's every Sunday of my life, and the only thing I have ever dropped into the

00:02:47.714 --> 00:02:48.740
Mire is a hymn-book.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:53.160
The stylus ran off the end and clicked, and clicked, and clicked.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:54.880
I did not lift it.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.020
I sat down upon the bed with my hands between my knees and listened to the clicking.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.240
The lamp began to gutter.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.520
The yellow ring shrank on the glass.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.560
And the horn, though it was silent, went on saying sit down now.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.420
I found Mr.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.621
Wetherby in the passage by the parlour door the next morning,

00:03:15.621 --> 00:03:19.400
trimming the wick of the hall lamp with a pair of small silver scissors.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.460
I had not slept.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:26.875
I had carried the cylinder down in my coat pocket and I held it out to him in my

00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:30.500
palm, as one holds out a coin to a beggar one does not trust.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.820
"Someone has been at my machine," I said.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:36.480
"There is a voice on this.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:37.600
It is mine.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.360
It speaks of a drowning."

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.920
He did not look at the cylinder.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.847
He looked at my face, and then he smiled, slowly, with the lips only,

00:03:46.847 --> 00:03:50.860
and set the scissors down upon the shelf beside the barometer.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.640
"You are pale, Mr.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.340
Marchbanks.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.180
The fog gets into the sleeping-rooms.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.240
I have always said so.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:03:59.960
He took out his watch and opened it.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:02.320
"The quarter-day is the twenty-fifth.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.731
Your father's sum stands at forty-one pounds, six shillings, and I am a patient man,

00:04:07.731 --> 00:04:09.520
but I am not a charitable one.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:10.960
Good morning."

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:13.160
He went into the parlour.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.681
The clock with the loose pendulum began its slow knocking behind the door,

00:04:17.681 --> 00:04:21.576
and I stood in the passage with the cylinder in my hand until the lamp,

00:04:21.576 --> 00:04:24.320
which he had trimmed, burned smokeless and steady.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.740
The next night there was another on the sill.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.954
It lay in the dust beside the window-catch, brown and fine-ribbed,

00:04:30.954 --> 00:04:33.160
and the window was latched from within.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.900
I told myself I would not play it.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:38.480
I played it before the church clock struck eleven.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:41.400
It was my voice again, and quieter.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.552
It said that the sexton, old Pettigrew,

00:04:44.552 --> 00:04:47.721
would cough three times during the Tuesday matins,

00:04:47.721 --> 00:04:50.700
and that the third cough would break the Creed.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.300
It said that Mr.

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:56.666
Wetherby would stop me on the stairs at noon and name forty-three pounds,

00:04:56.666 --> 00:04:58.580
not forty-one, for the interest.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:03.040
Then it said, I did not mean him to go under, Reginald.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:04.940
I took hold of his sleeve.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.240
It was wet wool, and it came away in my hand.

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:13.640
On Tuesday Pettigrew coughed three times, and the third broke the Creed.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:19.160
At noon, on the stairs, a hand touched my elbow, and a dry voice said,

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.840
"Forty-three pounds, Mr.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.520
Marchbanks.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:23.920
I did not answer.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.680
I went up and found the fourth cylinder waiting.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:28.780
So it went for seven days.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:32.934
Each night a brown cylinder; each day its prophecy,

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:35.400
kept as faithfully as a tide-table.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:39.772
The cooper's dog; the broken rung of the belfry ladder;

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:43.900
the very word Wetherby used for my lateness, which was negligent.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.720
And between the prophecies the drowning grew.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:52.240
It had a quay now, and a lantern, and the name of the Mire's lock-keeper.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.680
It had a boy's cap floating.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:59.791
My own tongue spoke of the hand going under with such tenderness that I caught

00:05:59.791 --> 00:06:05.176
myself, on the sixth night, with my palm laid flat against the horn as against a

00:06:05.176 --> 00:06:05.776
cheek.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.200
On the seventh night I did not wind the machine.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:15.023
I sat in the dark and waited, and the stylus lowered itself into the wax of its own

00:06:15.023 --> 00:06:15.623
accord.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:21.660
I carried all seven cylinders to Fothergill's door in the crook of my arm,

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:26.380
wrapped in my muffler like a litter of something sickly, and knocked with my knee.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.560
It was past one in the morning.

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:33.032
He opened at once, in his shirtsleeves, with a pen still in his hand,

00:06:33.032 --> 00:06:36.640
as though he had been expecting me and had not minded the wait.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.700
"Marchbanks," he said, in the low voice he used for everything,

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:42.960
even for the weather.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:44.420
"Come in.

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:46.560
You look like a man who has been bailing."

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:49.960
His room was the twin of mine, but warmer.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:53.949
He had a rag rug, a kettle on the hob, and on the table,

00:06:53.949 --> 00:06:58.420
under a square of green baize, a machine of his own with a japanned horn.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.760
I set the cylinders down in a row.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:02.620
I told him what was on them.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:08.545
I told it badly, out of order, the lock-keeper before the cap and the cap before the

00:07:08.545 --> 00:07:12.713
quay, and he listened with his head a little to one side, nodding,

00:07:12.713 --> 00:07:14.860
and poured me tea I did not drink.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:17.780
"Play them," I said.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:19.120
"Play any.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.960
Tell me whose voice it is."

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:22.920
He played the first.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:27.600
I watched his face while the wax turned, and there was nothing in it but patience.

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:34.133
When the drowning began, the tender plea of Desmond Marchbanks asking pardon,

00:07:34.133 --> 00:07:37.200
he closed his eyes as a man does at a hymn.

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.029
Then he lifted the stylus and played the fourth, and the sixth,

00:07:41.029 --> 00:07:45.040
and let the seventh run until the wet sleeve came away in my hand.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:48.240
"It is you," he said gently.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:50.420
"I will not pretend otherwise.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.580
But think, my dear fellow.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.440
Who wound the machine?

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.760
Who set the cylinder to the horn?

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:02.300
Wetherby's is an old man's voice, and an old man's voice is an easy thing to dream."

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:06.160
"Pettigrew coughed three times," I said.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:07.840
"The Creed broke."

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:11.060
"Pettigrew coughs three times every Tuesday.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:13.880
So does the Mire, I sometimes think.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.340
He smiled, and laid his hand on the baize.

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.440
"You walk, Desmond.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.009
I have heard your boots on the landing at three in the morning,

00:08:23.009 --> 00:08:25.240
and your talk through the wall, going on and on.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.340
The Larkspur has always made its lodgers strange.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.100
The man who had your room before you kept a hat-box of teeth.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.600
Sleep, and eat something, and leave the machine alone."

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:39.000
I wanted to believe him.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:43.434
I believed him all the way down the passage, with the muffler empty on my arm,

00:08:43.434 --> 00:08:47.513
for he had kept the cylinders, saying he would listen to them again by daylight and

00:08:47.513 --> 00:08:48.840
tell me what he made of it.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:51.640
The key turned stiffly in my door.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:55.139
The lamp, when I lit it, burned low and yellow,

00:08:55.139 --> 00:08:59.776
and I lay on the bed in my coat with the damp of the Mire coming up through the

00:08:59.776 --> 00:09:00.480
floorboards.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.240
I did not sleep.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:07.468
Toward four I rose to ease my head against the cold of the window,

00:09:07.468 --> 00:09:10.268
and the lamp swung my shadow across the room,

00:09:10.268 --> 00:09:13.940
and I saw the phonograph as I had not seen it in nine days.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:17.100
The brass horn did not point to the room.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.898
It lay turned against the wall, its mouth pressed to the paper,

00:09:21.898 --> 00:09:26.800
canted a hand's breadth out of true, as if it had been set there to listen.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:33.097
Beneath it, on the boards, lay a small grey drift of plaster dust,

00:09:33.097 --> 00:09:35.240
fine and fresh and unswept.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:36.920
I knelt.

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:38.900
I put my finger in it.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:40.500
It was still faintly damp.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.800
I took the horn in both hands and pulled.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.332
It came away from the paper with a small dry sound,

00:09:48.332 --> 00:09:50.960
and a crust of plaster fell across my knuckles.

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:54.697
Behind it, where the wall should have been solid,

00:09:54.697 --> 00:09:56.987
there was a hole the width of a florin,

00:09:56.987 --> 00:09:59.630
and in the hole the dull gleam of a tin tube,

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:01.920
wired to a lath with a twist of copper.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.780
I put my ear to it.

00:10:04.300 --> 00:10:05.300
The tube was cold.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:10.799
It breathed up at me the smell of a coal fire and of tobacco gone stale in a pipe,

00:10:10.799 --> 00:10:14.700
and from far below, very faint, came the tick of a clock I knew.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.858
It was the clock on Wetherby's parlour mantel,

00:10:17.858 --> 00:10:21.820
the one with the cracked enamel face that he wound each Sunday after chapel.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:27.455
I stayed there on my knees, and I counted the ticks as I have counted the strokes of

00:10:27.455 --> 00:10:31.920
the great tenor on a feast day, and somewhere past two hundred I understood.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:33.920
He had been listening.

00:10:34.540 --> 00:10:36.820
Not for nine days, but for months.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.389
Every night that I had lain in this bed and spoken to my father, or to the water,

00:10:42.389 --> 00:10:45.333
or to nobody, the tube had carried it down to him,

00:10:45.333 --> 00:10:48.100
and he had sat in his chair and written it out.

00:10:48.920 --> 00:10:52.887
I thought of the mornings I had woken with my tongue dry and my throat raw,

00:10:52.887 --> 00:10:54.580
and had put it down to the damp.

00:10:55.240 --> 00:11:00.649
I thought of the plea on the cylinder, tender and wheedling: forgive me, Desmond,

00:11:00.649 --> 00:11:03.120
say you forgive me, say you remember.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.366
I knew at last who had spoken it, because I heard it again in my head with the soft

00:11:08.366 --> 00:11:09.440
vowels laid bare.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:15.372
It was the gentle, patient, reasonable manner of the man who had just sent me to bed

00:11:15.372 --> 00:11:18.660
with a kind word and my own muffler empty on my arm.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:21.720
Alec Fothergill had begged me to remember.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.400
He had begged so sweetly that I had almost obliged him.

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.900
I did not weep, and I did not shout.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.540
I remember being surprised at how orderly my hands were.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:36.494
I rose, and I took off my boots and set them side by side under the bed,

00:11:36.494 --> 00:11:38.640
as a man does who means to be back.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:43.780
Then I put my hand into the breast of my coat and drew out the bell-rope knife.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.460
It had a short blade, bone-handled, worn thin as a leaf on the whetstone.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.718
I had cut a thousand ends of rope with it,

00:11:52.718 --> 00:11:55.800
and I had never once held it for any other purpose.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:57.800
I held it now.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:03.256
I turned it to the window and the grey began to lie along the edge,

00:12:03.256 --> 00:12:09.198
and I said aloud, quite quietly, "I have drowned nobody," and the tube in the wall

00:12:09.198 --> 00:12:11.880
took the words and carried them down.

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:16.720
I unlocked the door and opened it on its stiff hinge, a half-inch at a time.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.560
The stair ran down into the dark, and I went down it in my stockings,

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:24.800
one hand on the wall, the knife held against my thigh.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:30.560
The sixth tread cried out and I stood on it, and stood, until the house settled.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:35.580
Below me, under the parlour door, lay a long thin line of lamplight.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:36.960
He was awake.

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:42.124
At four in the morning, in a house of sleepers, Reginald Wetherby was awake,

00:12:42.124 --> 00:12:44.360
and waiting, and I heard him turn a page.

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:49.144
I pushed the door, and it went inward without a sound,

00:12:49.144 --> 00:12:51.340
as if it had been oiled for the purpose.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.400
The parlour was warm.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.622
A fire of sea-coal burned low in the grate,

00:12:56.622 --> 00:13:01.440
and the lamp stood on the table at his elbow, turned up high and trimmed clean.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:07.041
Reginald Wetherby sat in the horsehair chair with a ledger open across his knee and

00:13:07.041 --> 00:13:09.040
a cup of tea going cold on the arm.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:10.580
He did not rise.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:14.080
He did not so much as lift the hand that held the page.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:20.332
He looked at the knife, and then at my stockinged feet, and then he sighed,

00:13:20.332 --> 00:13:24.300
as a man sighs at a clock that has been wrongly wound.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:27.200
"You will want to put that down, Mr.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:29.940
Marchbanks, before you cut yourself on your own conclusions.

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:31.920
Sit, if you like.

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:34.240
The chair by the dresser is sound."

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.600
I did not sit.

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:39.980
I said, "You have been listening to me sleep."

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:43.320
"Eleven months," said Wetherby.

00:13:43.320 --> 00:13:45.060
"You talk a great deal, for a quiet man.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:49.660
Your father's debt, the bell, a boat, the black water off the Mire stairs.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:50.960
Mr.

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:52.460
Fothergill has a gift for arrangement.

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:55.840
He took what you gave us and made it speak in order."

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.900
"There was no drowning."

00:13:58.720 --> 00:13:59.760
"There was a confession.

00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:01.680
He turned a leaf.

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:04.740
"Your father's note is a curious instrument, Mr.

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:05.320
Marchbanks.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.780
It may be called in from a ringer of St.

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:12.880
Anselm's only if that ringer has stood convicted, or confessed, of a crime.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.640
I did not draw it.

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:15.940
I merely hold it.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:19.520
A man must be patient, and then he must be helpful."

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:21.940
"I never signed anything."

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:27.100
"You signed on the fourteenth, in the vestry, a receipt for the new sally.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:28.640
You were very tired.

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:33.248
The paper beneath it was a fair copy of what you had dictated to us,

00:14:33.248 --> 00:14:36.500
in your own voice, every night since Michaelmas.

00:14:36.500 --> 00:14:36.900
Mr.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:40.600
Fothergill read it into the horn and you answered, and I wrote it down.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:42.920
He closed the ledger on his finger.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.740
"It was sold to the magistrate yesterday afternoon.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.020
He is an early man.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:48.360
He will be here at dawn."

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.780
I think I raised the knife.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:55.440
I know that Wetherby watched it rise, and that he did not move.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.780
The fire ticked in the grate.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:01.781
I understood, with perfect orderly clearness, that he was not afraid,

00:15:01.781 --> 00:15:04.600
because there was nothing left in me that he needed to fear.

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.060
I ran.

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.260
The sixth tread cried out and I did not stop for it.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:14.440
I reached the landing, and the garret door stood open as I had left it.

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:19.243
I had one foot across the sill when I heard the stair behind me take a slow,

00:15:19.243 --> 00:15:22.800
deliberate weight, and the door came away from my hand and shut.

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:24.720
The key turned.

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.089
I heard it go round twice, and then withdrawn,

00:15:28.089 --> 00:15:31.720
and then the steady descent of a man who has no reason to hurry.

00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:33.500
I sat on the bed.

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:36.813
The window had gone the colour of old pewter,

00:15:36.813 --> 00:15:39.140
and the fog pressed its face to the glass.

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:43.160
I laid the knife in my lap, blade toward my knees.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.800
On the sill the phonograph clicked.

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:51.597
The stylus lifted from its rest, swung out, and dropped by itself into the wax,

00:15:51.597 --> 00:15:53.829
and my own voice, tender and ruined,

00:15:53.829 --> 00:15:57.300
began once more to say how sorry I was for the drowning.

